# Changelog

Corrections and rule-implementation changes are added here as new dated entries. Past records are never edited.

- **2026-11-24:** The setups position-size check now prices a stock setup at the price it would fill at (its trigger for buy-limit and buy-stop setups, the last price for at-open setups, plus slippage) instead of the prior close. This applies from the Tue 11/24 13:30 PT setup run (setups for Wed 11/25) on. The 10% position cap is unchanged. Setups committed earlier, and their rejections, stand as recorded.
- **2026-11-24:** A stock buy-limit setup whose order limit equals its trigger price now fills at the trigger plus slippage, the same as a buy-limit with no order limit. Before this, the fill rule (trigger plus slippage) always landed just above such a limit, so the setup could trigger but never fill. A fill is still never better than the trigger. An order limit above the trigger works as before, and one below the trigger is still refused. This applies to setups for Fri 11/27 on, so the first fill run it can affect is Fri 11/27 06:45 PT. Setups for earlier sessions, and their receipts, stand as recorded.
- **2026-11-24:** The Tue 11/24 09:30 PT fill run crashed before checking any fund ("too many open files"), so 11/24 has 2 of its 3 scheduled fill runs (06:45 and 12:45 PT); no fund was checked for triggers or exits at 09:30. The cause was the price download opening a connection for every symbol at once. From the Wed 11/25 06:45 PT run on, it downloads one symbol at a time. No fill rule, price rule or past record changed; the 11/24 records stand as recorded.
- **2026-11-25:** The Rejected count and rule adherence now include setups rejected at commit time. Before this, those rejections were recorded in each fund's rejections log but left out of the count, so the leaderboard showed 0. Corrected: Warri Buffi 1 (GOOGL), Flamalio 1 (GLD), Markiquill 1 (JPM), Sosnoozle 1 (SPY); Flamalio's adherence is 50%, not 100%.
- **2026-11-26:** The public-copy check now fails, instead of flagging for a manual check, when a real investor's name is used as a person (followed by "says", "said", "writes", "calls" and similar, or a possessive such as "'s memo"). Funds are also told, from the Fri 11/27 13:30 PT setup run on, never to name, quote or paraphrase a real investor, fund manager or firm in their setup reasons, lessons or notes. Markiquill's committed notes for Fri 11/27 name a real investor. That committed record is hashed and stays exactly as recorded; how its public copy is handled is pending. No fill rule, price rule or past record changed.
